{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>And you shall see it and remember all the commandments of HaShem.</b> You shall remember that you are servants to the blessed El and that you accepted His commandments under oath and imprecation — this, upon seeing the tzitzit, which is like the king's seal upon his servants. And through this you will cease from wandering after your heart, to pursue the inclination of your heart for wealth and honor, even by means of theft." "<b>And after your eyes.</b> To attain the lusts upon which you have set your eyes." "<b>Which you go astraying after.</b> Bending your rational soul through them from the paths of eternal life to the paths of destruction and death."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:59.874562590Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}